{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
  "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Connie L. Lensing",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress clearly set out a statutory scheme in which timely notice and the opportunity for conciliation are required before an age discrimination private suit may be brought."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, EEOC Form 5 is labelled \"Charge.\" And would it be your position that if an employee filled out that form and submitted it to the EEOC, but the EEOC made a mistake and did not notify the employer, that that would not be a charge?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel, the Government relied in its brief very heavily on the Chevron case, saying we should defer to the agency's regulations, and on the Auer case, saying we defer to the agency to tell us what its regulations mean. And you didn't cite either of those cases in your reply brief. So I wonder what your answer is to that argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. LENSING",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. LENSING: Well, the -- the regulations are certainly entitled to deference, and taken as a whole, the regulations, just as the statutes, require notice. But what the EEOC's position is, is the regulations that describe what a charge is are not enough, and the entire definition is not embodied in the regulations. You have to go to -- to memos we wrote and to a compliance manual, which is not in the record and is not attached to the brief and is not available to"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But if they do that why can't -- and you don't -- if they don't give you the notice, well, then you can complain, they didn't give us the notice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why do you think -- why do you think they must have lost it? Why did you think they must have lost it: Because she hadn't been given a number?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rose",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem with EEOC is, when they get a new thing that's not a Form 5, they don't docket it. This didn't get docketed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What I think Miss Lensing, one of her more basic points is this: There is a statute. And the statute says the EEOC shall send prompt notice in part to the conciliation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0002-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF TOBY J. HEYTENS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES AS AMICUS CURIAE SUPPORTING THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The word \"manifest intent\" is not set forth expressly there."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is a complaint different from an intake questionnaire?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just to get one thing perfectly clear in my mind, does that mean if the intake questionnaire is checked not consent, that would not be a charge?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Connie L. Lensing)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of all, in this case the affidavit attached to the intake questionnaire began -- and this is at Joint Appendix 266 -- with the statement, \"I have been assured of confidentiality by the EEOC.\" So it is a confidentiality concern. Congress determined that there must be an opportunity for conciliation before a lawsuit was filed. We never saw the numbers that are not in the record, that were testified to today, but if 247 charges were filed against FedEx, in that period of time we had 25 age discrimination cases. So conciliation before a case does work. And I appreciate those numbers because it -- it just shows that we conciliate, we look into it, but you can't do it once the lawsuit is filed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: How do we fix it? You haven't gotten notice, you haven't had a chance to conciliate -- how do we fix it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1322",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8be5ec2bc1d71a65ad6e29dbca8c3354eab9a2b1c25a661cacfd62561b65b7db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8be5ec2bc1d7-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Miss Lensing. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 12:04 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
